# Cursor pointer on clickable controls

Every interactive control that the user can click must show the **pointer** (hand) cursor on hover.

## Do

- Put `cursor-pointer` on buttons, close/dismiss controls (`Sheet`/`Dialog` X), icon-only actions, **collapse/expand triggers** (group headers, expand-all / collapse-all), tabs triggers used as buttons, and custom `<button>` / `role="button"` elements.
- Prefer baking it into shared primitives (`Button`, Sheet/Dialog close) so callers inherit it.
- Disabled controls: `disabled:cursor-not-allowed` (and keep non-interactive).

## Do NOT

- Leave close buttons or ghost/icon buttons without `cursor-pointer` (default arrow looks broken).
- Rely on browser default for `<button>` alone when Tailwind/`button` reset may leave `cursor: default`.

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ Sheet / Dialog close
<SheetPrimitive.Close className="… cursor-pointer …">

// ✅ Custom icon button
<button type="button" className="… cursor-pointer …">

// ❌ Missing pointer
<SheetPrimitive.Close className="absolute top-4 right-4 opacity-70 …">
```

`Button` (`components/ui/button.tsx`) already includes `cursor-pointer`. Raw Radix closes and one-off `<button>`s do **not** — always add it.
